{"scope":"Exact known-component propagation under the GLOBAL hypothesis c>=4.\n\nFor any triangle L in srg(99,14,1,2), its outside neighbourhood has36\nvertices in three colour classes. Each vertex has exactly one neighbour\nin each colour, including its own. Every connected component therefore\nhas equally many vertices of each colour and its order is a multiple of6.\nAt least four components force every component to have at most18 vertices.\n\nA known connected component exceeding18 vertices (or six of one colour)\nis impossible. A known18-component is closed: every edge to another known\nneighbour of L is zero. Its known neighbours outside it cannot acquire\nan edge to L. These implications are interleaved with exact C1/C2 binary\npropagation. This is unavailable without the global c>=4 hypothesis.\n","global_minimum_components":4,"source":"data\\codex_partial_star_20261018\\c4_9_193_fixed_domain_kernel.json","template_index":9,"gram_index":193,"uses_fixed_gram":false,"component_codes":[[0,4,8],[0,4,13],[1,4,7],[1,4,8],[1,4,10],[1,4,13],[2,3,11],[2,3,14],[7,4,4],[7,4,5],[7,4,8],[7,4,9],[7,4,10],[7,4,13],[25,1,11],[25,1,14],[26,0,11],[26,0,14],[36,0,11],[36,0,14],[38,0,10],[127,4,4],[127,4,5],[127,4,8],[127,4,13],[304,0,0],[305,0,0],[316,0,0],[317,0,0],[323,0,0],[333,0,0]],"results":[{"component_index":0,"code":[0,4,8],"status":"UNRESOLVED","rounds":[{"known_triangles":61,"closed18_components":[{"line":[0,1,2],"component":[9,10,11,12,13,14,21,22,23,24,25,26,33,34,35,36,37,38],"colour_counts":[6,6,6]}],"maximum_known_component_vertices":18,"new_zeros":0}],"added_zeros":{},"fixed_edges":1620,"binary_conflict":null},{"component_index":1,"code":[0,4,13],"status":"UNRESOLVED","rounds":[{"known_triangles":61,"closed18_components":[{"line":[0,1,2],"component":[9,10,11,12,13,14,21,22,23,24,25,26,33,34,35,36,37,38],"colour_counts":[6,6,6]}],"maximum_known_component_vertices":18,"new_zeros":0}],"added_zeros":{},"fixed_edges":1620,"binary_conflict":null},{"component_index":2